{#- Cover of article 07, drawn with the theme's colours. Decorative: the title
    sits next to it. A packet as a relay sees it, inside a viewfinder: the
    clear header cells, then the sealed payload (hatched, with a padlock).
    The mailbox field (accent) carries an ID and its day number. Below, a
    tag on the connection holds the client's IP address (threat colour, a
    documentation address from RFC 5737). Motion, once, only without reduced
    motion: the day turns twice and the mailbox ID changes with it, while the
    IP tag stays exactly as it was, which is the article's point. No
    transport colours: nothing here travels between relays. Only the day
    label follows the page language. -#}
{%- set dayWord = 'jour' if lang == 'fr' else 'day' -%}
